-## Why an extension
-S09:153-158 already binds local originalMethod, target and firstRequestId before super.fetch; firstConnectionCalls records an arrival including metadata. S09:352 firstConnectionProbe reads the entire list plus business inventory/alarm and a shared catch buffer. Its contents and reads exceed this task. The existing response reaction observes only POST. S09:351,383-391 catch frames are neither GET progress nor uniquely joined completion. c2ScopeState/drop requires a separate POST epoch. Even their simultaneous absence supplies no negative proof. GB1 b97a7415951e7fe4ecb988a921cc0d777ea18f35 and 08b75777bb39efaad0a439082cd430044c0b07d6 already qualify ordinary inert actor success and selected faults. Reuse this evidence. Add one narrow QA query on the existing isolated actor plus one independently named private response metadata field carrying the exact M record across dispatch. Do not change g1, C2FT4, OWN, any product method or any product response. This explicit fixture transport change needs independent approval. The QA read is the only added cross-isolate post-result query. The private metadata is written in the diagnostic M overlay and locally decoded by the fixture host after the original count. No header/status/body read is added to the measured M or QA operation.
