-On the M actual path store two independent small enums: last normally resumed original await, and current original site. Start last=NONE. Mark a site immediately before its original await/call and update last at the first statement after normal await resumption, before subsequent checks. A throwing or still-pending await never becomes last. For the nominated no-body GET cover bridge:26 (request bytes), :36 (stub fetch), :41 (response bytes), and wire:43-49 (each original reader.read return, and existing error-path reader.cancel), :51-53 (existing error-body cancel). Request/response readers use distinct site enums; repeated reads reuse the same finite code. Use one weak association to the exact message from this bound original invocation so the shared wire helper can update only its caller's private cell. Put a separate site marker immediately before synchronous validation and a validation-success marker only after original return; they never become await completions. The finite operation and outer bridge/worker wrappers await this race/bridge, respectively: those outer returns have not occurred at its winning callback and cannot be its last inner completion. Instrument no new await, promise reaction, timer, clock, body/header/status access, cancellation or waitUntil. Do not replace or reconstruct errors, responses, promises, abort signals, scopes or deadlines.
