-Keep one original callback registered on the same two sources, the same reference for lease add/remove and setTimeout, same duration/once/cleanup/order. Bind its actual call arguments (regular invocation-local arguments, not arrow lexical arguments). At these two closed callsites only, zero callback arguments designate the timer registration, the sole event argument designates the signal registration; any other shape/provenance is UNKNOWN. Prove the distinction on the nominated native platform with independent timer-only and signal-only controls. No reading signal.aborted/event getters after the race, no finding a source from elapsed time. Lease event origin remains UNKNOWN (root timer vs inbound). Bind {source,last,site,key} by exact error identity immediately before original reject(error). Keep immutable candidate facts for the bounded original registration invocations (max two). At S09:739-745 choose only the snapshot for the identical escaping error and matching lease; at :746-765 require same caught error and original pending Response as g1. Never sample mutable progress at catch. The later callback, retained work, parent.finish or a later error cannot rewrite that snapshot. A different original winner keeps its existing category; source is UNKNOWN unless the deadline fact matched. No new status reads: reuse validated locals and original headers object in existing finish only. A fixture-reserved separate header can be set there on the internally constructed pending response, after unchanged g1 handling, when g1 itself validated the deadline; absent on all other responses. Only this test-owned response factory can emit it, with literal preimage/hash check for no prior occurrences. Never overwrite caller/stub metadata or emit through negative/real workers. No extra public g1 field. Wire bytes for the private record capped at 128 ASCII (bounded numeric enums and optional 36-byte UUID), no URLs, times, IDs of resources, error data or secrets.
