-## QA | bounded state and a later sample
-S09:153-158 fixture superclass wrapper already captures exact request and ID synchronously. At entry (before original super.fetch), admit only the fixed target and original GET from existing captured scalars. Feed a new per-actor in-memory registry plus a WeakMap keyed by the actual Request. Capture that cell in the existing reaction closure; never look up mutable this.firstRequestId later. Only the existing reaction is used. Mark its fulfillment or rejection by outcome alone, without touching response/status/body. This says wrapper fulfilled/rejected, not successful business work. S02:14-26 link exact request and receiving local lease synchronously, mark receiver accepted after original check; mark original handle await return on normal continuation. Link the reconstructed original Request at S00:636 to that same cell by identity before S01 sees it. Thread retained closure identity and explicit object links only in private helper state; no field added to request, lease, env, options or DTO. In nested readChoice (S00:641-652) use that invocation's lexical request; multiple concurrent invocations cannot borrow a slot. Use separate fixed lane variables for outer work and nested owned timeline so a nested read never overwrites its enclosing site.
