-For each listed await mark ENTER immediately before the original expression and NORMAL_RETURN immediately after its normal resumption using captured scalars only. S00:635,637,642,652 delimit BODY, INITIAL_PHASE_PAIR, OWNED_TIMELINE, CHOICE. S01:212,214,217,221,228-232 delimit PREVIOUS_TICKET/STAGE_CONTEXT or RESOLVE, LIMIT, SNAPSHOT_PAIR, PROJECT_PAIR, TICKET_PAIR, FINAL_OWN and FINAL_CHECK. Use separate levels for top-level QA handler, choice step and recurring owned timeline. Report only last normal enum and currently entered enum per level; successive calls may repeat. If a normal awaited assignment is followed immediately by a check on that source line, insert the observation between those operations. Mark form constructed only after original new Response succeeds at S00:659; leave catch/denial returns distinguishable from normal form creation. Failure state means a matched original catch/receiver/wrapper failure observed, without reading error data; do not imply failed validation or a receipt from normal promise fulfillment. Once wrapper settles, freeze record. Retained late descendants cannot update it or imply drain. In the fixture overlay only, add a fixed sparse cursor within S00 observeOwnerPhasePair, bound to its invocation by the original parent/lexical child association (initial parent and exact readChoice call, no ambient "current QA"). At :196,275,512 identify FACTS, PRIMARY, QUALIFY and round 1/2 at original callsites. At :169-193 mark the original awaited callsites covering anchors, selection, backup/receipt/chunk, inventories, issuer/SDK/notice/cleanup; repeated backup chunk uses the same site ID. :205-275 separates credential join and QA/M primary join; :279-512 identifies the native journal/selection/notice-read and qualification callsites. For each selected callsite, immediately before its unaltered await set its numeric pending site, immediately after normal return set last and increment a bounded count. Use the original statements and evaluation order, no wrapping promises or arguments. Parallel producer branches use distinct fixed lanes (reader/publisher for credentials; QA/M for primary) bound by closure; keep per-lane pending site and last normal site, count in one fixed struct. No shared scalar that implies serial order of concurrent operations. For parallel helpers that return a promise directly, use the existing caller's await or existing join; never add a reaction to observe a plain return. If individual completion is unobservable below a join, only JOIN_WAIT/RETURN and actually observed lane sites are reportable. Within each of at most 255 observed pair invocations, track saturating round and one cumulative normal-return count across the invocation, max 65535. Preserve final cursor while later outer sites run; mark inactive so stale leaf data cannot be treated as outstanding. Report pair invocation number, round, group, pending lane mask, four fixed lane cells and completed count as a single bounded packed tuple alongside the outer site. Cursor may show e.g. many sequential completions and a later entered chunk ordinal. A single sample cannot measure advancement rate, prove a read is slow/stuck, or place any QA return at M's cutoff. An entered lane selects the static leaf and surrounding original deadline for review; with no positive join or overflow, leave QA UNKNOWN. Business logic and storage operations are identical; no extra reads to inspect keys, paths, results or credentials. No GET or private authorization data (cookies, tokens, owner, values, response text, storage, snapshots) may be read for this diagnostic.
