-## Host and the single read
-S08:17-19 captures the original Response/status after the existing original text read; retain only the Response reference for the unique case15 label and same main/direct mounted dispatch with S09:830-860's existing guards. Preserve original assertion, returned error and case result. S08:215-231 leaves original count and C2FT4 exactly intact. Add an outer fixture driver step only after the original count promise has successfully returned and before teardown/next action. Hold the existing label association independently before it is consumed. If no completed count or exact original response/label/mount, emit UNKNOWN; do not substitute a different count. The fixture host now obtains only the single private field from that retained exact Response (host-local decode post-cut; no read in the measured work). Admit only the matching g1 deadline/status and strict private shape. Use the same fixed actor stub from S10:169-171,188-200. Make one fixture-only read for the exact key, capped at 256 serialized bytes and 1000 ms host budget, one attempt, no polling, retry, probe, batch, enumeration, confirmation, or route discovery. Timer outside measured operation, disposed after read; losing or subsequently resolving RPC is ignored, without claiming cancellation. It returns a copy of the bounded record, never clears/arms or advances it. Actor never trusts the key for permission. Isolate privately mounted in a credential-free fixture with no external traffic. Host checks schema, epoch and returned key, then strips key/epoch from emitted evidence. Never read the old firstConnectionProbe. Missing/foreign/poisoned/disposed/over-budget/partial yields QA UNKNOWN. No-record is not no-delivery. Later actor read is not an atomic distributed snapshot: its facts mean "observed in this invocation by later fixture read". Ordering of those facts relative to the M cutoff is always UNKNOWN, unless a fixture-only control supplies separate causal ordering for that control alone.
