-## One independent output
-Private evidence file, single row, closed schema AFW.PENDING.GET/1, maximum 1024 UTF-8 bytes, no unknown keys, dynamic string or arrays. label fixed case15; cut = M_ESCAPING_CALLBACK or UNKNOWN; mLast/mSite/mInput finite enums above or UNKNOWN; qaBasis = LATER_SINGLE_READ or UNKNOWN; qaArrival = OBSERVED or UNKNOWN; qaReceiver, qaForm = OBSERVED or UNKNOWN; qaOuterLast/At, qaChoiceLast/At, qaTimelineLast/At carry mapped enum or NONE/UNKNOWN; wrapper = FULFILLED/REJECTED/OPEN_AT_READ/UNKNOWN; qaPair = UNKNOWN or fixed numeric tuple (pair ordinal, round, group, active bit, last site, pending site, cumulative normal count, pending lane mask, four fixed lane last/entered pairs; fixed fields, no variable-length data), qaVsMTime = UNKNOWN always; quality = JOINED/M_ONLY/UNKNOWN, reason = OK/ABSENT/UNJOINED/OVERLAP/TRUNCATED/STALE/TIMEOUT/INVALID/NO_CUT/OTHER_WINNER. NONE means intact instrumented level entered with no normally returned await yet; an unobserved level is UNKNOWN. OPEN_AT_READ means a positive entry with no observed settlement at that local snapshot, not an independently detected stall. Local PRIVATE wire uses compact finite numeric enums, fixed known build epoch and optional UUID; check encoded lengths before accepting. Include only the fixed progress ordinal/count in the final cursor; exclude any transport-integrity counters. Independent host accepts only combinations reachable in the specified state machine. Never use the row for admission or a successful product assertion.
